UnitMetaquoter::QuoteRemoveLiquidityV2
├── when the pool is not a registered target
│   └── it reverts with IP
└── given the pool is a registered target
    ├── when the target factory is not approved
    │   └── it reverts with AF
    └── given the target factory is approved
        ├── when the total supply is zero
        │   └── it returns amount0 and amount1 as zero
        └── given the total supply is nonzero
            ├── when the liquidity exceeds the total supply
            │   └── it reverts with LTS
            ├── when the liquidity exceeds the supply held outside the pool
            │   └── it reverts with LTS
            ├── when a pool balance exceeds its reserve
            │   └── it quotes from the reserves
            ├── when pool balances are below reserves
            │   └── it returns amount0 and amount1 proportional to the pool's live balances
            ├── when one balance exceeds its reserve and the other is below
            │   └── it caps each side independently
            ├── when a stable pool would have zero residual k
            │   └── it reverts with KZ
            ├── when a stable pool retains a nonzero residual k
            │   └── it returns amount0 and amount1 proportional to the pool's live balances
            ├── when either amount rounds to zero
            │   └── it reverts with ILB
            └── when the pool already holds liquidity
                └── it reverts with KZ
